  "text_sanskrit": "नान्यं गुणेभ्यः कर्तारं यदा द्रष्टानुपश्यति । गुणेभ्यश्च परं वेत्ति मद्भावं सोऽधिगच्छति ॥ १४-१९ ॥",
  "itrans": "nAnya.n guNebhyaH kartAraM yadA draShTAnupashyati . guNebhyashcha paraM vetti madbhAvaM so.adhigachChati .. 14-19 ..",
  "translation": "When the seer (Jiva) clearly perceives that nothing else than the Trigunas is the modifying cause and also that (i.e., Myself) which is the cause higher than the Trigunas, he attains to the state of being in Me. (19)\nV. The cause higher: the independent and efficient cause. The state of being in Me: the blissful state of resting in Me.\nAnother interpretation. Now the first word in the verse is Nâ=man. To translate again: When Jiva the seer perceives the Maker to be different from the Gunas, then he is man (otherwise he is a beast). (This is not enough, but he should know more). He who knows the Maker to be far higher than the qualities — he attains to the state of being in Me: (19.) \nA. Thus the mundane bondage, a mingling of pleasure and pain, is the effect of the Trigunas. Only when they are rooted out, the bondage also will go-which the following verse declares.",
